### Bug Scenario Description and Root Cause

The bug report describes an issue where using `hash-type: number` in a Reveal.js presentation misaligns the title slide. The images provided show the difference between using `hash-type: number` and `hash-type: title`. With `hash-type: number`, the title slide is not centered, while it is correctly centered with `hash-type: title`.

The root cause of the issue is likely related to how the `id` attribute is handled for the title slide when `hash-type: number` is used. The code snippet indicates that the `id` attribute is removed from the title slide when `hash-type: number` is specified, which may interfere with the CSS or JavaScript logic responsible for centering the slide.

### Bug Location and Analysis

The relevant code snippet is in the file `src/format/reveal/format-reveal.ts`. The section of interest is:

```javascript
// if we are using 'number' as our hash type then remove the
// title slide id
if (format.metadata[kHashType] === "number") {
  const titleSlide = doc.getElementById("title-slide");
  if (titleSlide) {
    titleSlide.removeAttribute("id");
  }
}
```

This code removes the `id` attribute from the title slide when `hash-type: number` is used, which likely causes the misalignment.

